small_email: Zombie-style proximity policy on Enron email.

Policy, faithful to Zombie (NSDI'24) §6.3 proximity example:
  keyword R1 within 100 chars of R2, case-sensitive, dot-all,
  both directions.
  R1 = driving license | driver's license | DL   (shared keyword)
  R2 = Zombie's 5-arm Microsoft Purview DLP union, SPLIT into 5
       separate sigs (one PCRE subsig each, no trigger, logic "0"):
         Bora.Email.DLProx.Passport  [0-9a-zA-Z][0-9]{8}
         Bora.Email.DLProx.SSN       [0-9]{3}[-\s]?[0-9]{2}?[-\s]?[0-9]{4}
         Bora.Email.DLProx.License   ([0-9]{3}\s){2}[0-9]{3}
         Bora.Email.DLProx.Bank      [0-9]{6,17}
         Bora.Email.DLProx.ITIN      9[0-9]{2}[-\s]?(5[0-9]|6[0-5]|..)[-\s]?[0-9]{4}

main_dfa.dat lists ONLY the Win.Alphabet.SAMPLE-1 seed sig (cheap
hex DFA that seeds the 16-nibble alphabet). The 5 DLP sigs are NOT
in the DFA list -- building a DFA for the .{0,100} x 5-arm union is
too expensive; they go through the SED / pm-bounds path instead.

Scan target: data/samples/email_merged128k/merged_000020. It has
the keyword (x2) and the License "ddd ddd ddd" arm (x6) but no arm
match within 100 chars of a keyword -> clean under all 5 arms ->
discharges green while exercising the proximity prune.

Run: cargo test -p zkregplus -- test_small_email \
       --show-output --nocapture
